[b]A mod for Mount & Blade II: Bannerlord.[/b]

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

It separates dedicated skirmishers from heavy troops that carry just one or two throwables, like Legionaries and Menavliatons.

When a formation prefers [b]Throwing Weapons[/b] in the Order of Battle, troops are ranked by what they actually carry:
[list]
[*][b]two or more javelin stacks[/b] first
[*]then [b]one stack[/b]
[*]then [b]pila carriers[/b]
[/list]

[b]Settings[/b] (optional, with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu[/url]): turn it on or off, and set the minimum throwables a troop needs to count.

[h1]Requirements[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859188632]Harmony[/url] (required)
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] (optional)
[/list]

Safe to add or remove mid-campaign: it changes no save data.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Do whatever you like with it.
To thank me, open [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]my GitHub profile[/url] and read my top pinned.

Not on Steam? Download it from GitHub: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/better-skirmisher-separation]github.com/TraxData313/better-skirmisher-separation[/url]
